# Etrata, Deadly Fugitive: "{2}{U}{B}: Turn this creature face up. If you can't, exile it, then you may cast the exiled card without paying its mana cost." Bot1's face-down Dog Walker (Disguise, cast for {3} with
# Black Lotus on turn 1) is turned face up in response to the ability, with its own disguise cost {R/W}{R/W} (Mox Pearl and Plains), a special action (CR 116.2b, 702.168d): its "turned face up" trigger makes two Dogs.
# When the ability resolves (after the Dogs trigger) the Dog Walker is already face up, so it can't be turned face up: it is exiled and Bot1 may cast the exiled card free (CR 400.7: a new Dog Walker, face up, so no more Dogs).

